# Runtime state written into a config directory the moment the server (or
# `--create-token`) is pointed at it. All three are secrets in practice:
# .storage/auth.json holds token hashes, secrets.yaml holds the real ones, and
# jarvis.db knows when the house is empty and when the front door opened.
.storage/
secrets.yaml
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
